R-PA1 R-PA2 R-PA3 R-PA7 R-PA8 R-PA9 R-PA11 R-PA12 R-PA13 R-PA14 R-CM9 R-CM10 R-EC2 (slice 042, `tln patch`): 12 runs with the fake fetch. The index has `acme/json 2.1.0` (hash 3zDZ...6Wm, the files are in the cache of the home) and `acme/parser 1.0.0` (hash PKAo...bLbG, not in the cache: the fetch puts it there). p1 has no `talon.toml`, p2 has a `talon.toml` with comments, p3 has a copy with many edits, p4 has a `talon.toml` with `[dependencies]` only.
Run 1 (`patch json`, p1, no `talon.toml`): the copy is made in `.talon/patches/json/` (R-PA1, R-PA11: a normal dir in the tree). `talon.toml` is created with `[patch]` and the entry in the table form (R-PA9, R-PA1). The base is the hash of the base package. No diff file and no commit (R-PA2).
Run 2 (the same again): the copy dir exists: exit 2, nothing changes (R-PA1).
Run 3 (`patch pf`, the platform of the app): exit 2 (R-PA8). Run 4 (`patch util`, a path entry): exit 2 (R-PA14, R-CM10: unmanaged entry). Run 5 (`patch src`, a foreign URL): exit 2 (R-PA14).
Run 6 (`list`): the `json` row has the mark `patched` after the patch of run 1 (R-CM9). The other rows have no mark of this kind.
Run 7 (`patch parser`, p2, the package is not in the cache): the fetch is by hash (R-PA13). The existing `talon.toml` keeps its text: only the table `[patch]` is added at the end (R-PA1, R-PA9).
Run 8 (`patch json`, p2): the second key is added in the same `[patch]` table.
Run 9 (`patch parser --diff`, p2): no change against the base. The note is on stderr, stdout is empty, and nothing is written (R-PA3).
Run 10 (`patch json --diff`, p3): the unified diff of the copy against the base package (R-PA3, R-PA7): edits with 3 lines of context, two hunks that are far apart, a change at the end, an added file in a new dir, deleted files, an empty added file (no hunk), a file that gets its first line, a file that loses all lines, a final newline added, the last line changed with no final newline, a binary file (`Binary files ... differ`). The files are in byte order of the path. It writes nothing.
Run 11 (the same with `--json`): the envelope has `command` `patch` and `data` with the changes and the diff text (a proposal, TW24).
Run 12 (`patch json --json`, p4): `data` has `alias`, `name`, `version`, `base`, `dir`, `toml` and `toml_created` (a proposal, TW24). The entry is added to a `talon.toml` that exists (R-PA9).
Run 13 (`patch json --diff`, p5: a `talon.toml` with no `[patch]` key): exit 2, `json has no patch. Run tln patch json first.`, nothing is written (R-PA3, R-EC2; answer Q1).
Run 14 (`patch json --diff`, p6: a `[patch]` entry whose copy dir is missing): exit 2, the text names the dir (R-PA3, R-EC2; answer Q1).
Run 15 (`patch json --diff`, p7: the `base` of the entry is a hash that is not in the cache, and not the hash of the header entry): the base dir is missing: an `Environment` failure `cannot read <dir>` (gap test, the code agent decision Q7). Nothing is written.
